        "original_id": "8f196bec-a456-59c9-a189-3abe24027d2f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Archie Andrews, John L. Goldwater, Bob Montana, Vic Bloom, Fiona Staples, Mike Costa\n- Organizations: Archie Comics, WildStorm\n- Products: Archie, The Archie Show, Archie's Weird Mysteries, North 40, DV8: Gods and Monsters, T.H.U.N.D.E.R. Agents, Saga, Archie Andrews radio series\n- Topics: comic books, comic book artists\n\nFacts:\n- Archie Andrews was created in 1941 by publisher John L. Goldwater and artist Bob Montana in collaboration with writer Vic Bloom.\n- Archie Andrews is the main character in an American comic book series published by Archie Comics.\n- Archie Andrews also appeared in the long-running Archie Andrews radio series, a syndicated comic strip, The Archie Show, and Archie's Weird Mysteries.\n- Mike Costa's first published work was a 2008 title created with artist Fiona Staples for WildStorm.\n- Fiona Staples is a Canadian comic book artist known for work on North 40, DV8: Gods and Monsters, T.H.U.N.D.E.R. Agents, Archie, and Saga.\n- Archie, also known as Archie Comics, is an ongoing comic book series featuring the Archie Comics character Archie Andrews.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
